      "LOUISE: Hey -- nice shooting, soldier.\nSTELLA: How's the leg?",
      "LOUISE: Nice haircut.\nSTELLA: Looks like you're doing alright.",
      "LOUISE: What did these cost you? If you paid more than fifteen bucks you got ripped off.\nSTELLA: Y'know, if those papers turned out to be phony, we'd have to arrest you. . You could get six months.",
      "LOUISE: Isn't that an awfully rough place for you two to be hanging out?\nSTELLA: I hope you did better than that.",
      "STELLA: Really? I would've thought hookers and mud-wrestlers are just your speed.\nLOUISE: After you...\nSTELLA: Okay. Sit down here and be quiet.\nSTELLA: Relax, it's night maneuvers. Just pretend we're at a drive- in movie."
    ]
